// ## 6. Recommendation To Agy (Library Lane)
//
// The BLOCKED set has nothing for agy to fix. Specifically:
//
// 1. Do NOT look for BLOCKED rows you can unblock. There are none.
// 2. The 3-file split in handoff_library_split.oot is a FORMAT item. It does
//    not move any row from BLOCKED to GREEN. Library_status row text will
//    stay identical after the split (handoff_library_split.oot:21-22, 172-178).
// 3. If the owner wants library-lane work this cycle, finish the 3-file split
//    first. It is the only library work that touches the BLOCKED-adjacent
//    surface (dispatch_worker.oo is BLOCKED for compiler reasons; the split
//    does not unblock it, but it does keep FORMAT honest while the compiler
//    lane works).
// 4. The compiler lane should look at the c_emit defects in
//    hash/md5.oo, hash/sha1.oo, sec/cps/*.oo, sec/crypto/poly1305.oo,
//    sec/sys/cfi_engine.oo, sec/sys/elf.oo first. These are the densest
//    gcc-error sites and they cover the three top "need" categories
//    (A: oodac/C lower, C: emit-c exit 0, D: timeout 45s).
//
// Cross-references:
//   handoff_library_split.oot:21    lists the 3 oversized files and sizes.
//   handoff_library_split.oot:22    "Splitting reduces line count only. Prove status stays BLOCKED."
